## 🎯 Day 58 Objective

Days 53–57 produced five technical artefacts. None of them is presentable to a board — they are practitioner documents, and their depth is exactly what makes them unusable in a forty-minute governance slot.

This is the translation layer: **the whole stack compressed into fourteen slides a CISO or board audit committee would actually sit through**, structured as a decision document rather than an education document.

The test it was built against: a non-technical director should be able to follow why agentic AI is a different risk class, understand what it costs to address, and vote on four specific decisions — without needing any of the underlying material.

