## 📑 Slide Flow

| # | Slide | Job it does |
|---|-------|-------------|
| 1 | Title | Frames the asymmetry: systems act, controls haven't caught up |
| 2 | **Executive summary + the ask** | Three things to know, four decisions to make — lead with the ask, not the education |
| 3 | What changed | Generative vs agentic, side by side |
| 4 | The exposure | 74% adopting / 21% governed, plus the 74%/27% self-assessment delta |
| 5 | Why existing controls don't fire | Three structural reasons — justifies new investment rather than more of the same |
| 6 | Anatomy of a breach | Six moves, every step authorised |
| 7 | **Where to spend first** | 6 of 10 risks at two control points — the fundable insight |
| 8 | Target architecture | Control plane outside the agent; allow / deny / modify |
| 9 | Where we stand | Maturity bars + two failed hard gates |
| 10 | Incident reality | Containment ≠ eradication; notification clocks |
| 11 | Regulatory runway | Dec 2027, and how to spend fifteen months |
| 12 | **Four decisions** | Each with cost of yes *and* cost of no |
| 13 | Twelve-month sequence | Five phases, with the commonly-skipped one called out |
| 14 | The one sentence | Closes on the asymmetry |

**Design:** navy/amber palette, Cambria headers with Calibri body, numbered-circle motif carried throughout, dark slides bookending light content. Validated clean; every slide visually inspected.

